{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"aware-obvious-sphinx","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n30 pytest modules re-run a `scripts/check_*.py` gate over the real tree (\"the repository is clean\"), grep the `Makefile` for its invocation, and in several modules do both; the script already runs in `make lint` (`Makefile:266-439`), which CI runs via `_build-and-test.yml:102`, so a lint-wired script has one owner. The twin fails a second time for the same defect and doubles suite time for zero signal. Three scripts (`check_adr_numbers`, `check_docs_index`, `check_verify_gate_parity`) run only as CI steps (docs-gates action `:22` and `:59`; `_build-and-test.yml:145-152`), so their pytest twin is currently their only portable owner. Table (3), the single-owner table over all 33 scripts with the per-module delete and keep sets, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n- Delete the 74 collected nodes named in table (3) — the \"real tree is clean\", \"make lint wires it\" and \"runs the real script as a subprocess\" twins — from their modules; the `--strict-markers` `repo_policy` mark on deleted tests goes with them. Fixture tests on synthetic input are kept (per-module keep counts are in the table).\n- Delete `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` whole (6 wiring tests, 109 LOC).\n- Add `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` after `Makefile:439` (below the `check_verify_gate_parity.py` line S2 adds), so every lint-target script has `make lint` as its one owner.\n- Scripts that keep a non-lint owner lose only the twins the table names: `check_readme_quickstart` stays CI-owned (docs-gates `:70`, `test.yml:189`, `gerrit-verify.yaml:352`; it executes the quickstart); `check_build_env_locked` (`release.yml:184`), `check_commit_message_wrap` (pre-commit `:78-80`), `check_import_walk` (typecheck `:505`), `check_orphaned_load` (operator diagnostic, `docs/orphaned-processes.md`), `check_server_manifest` (`_build-and-test.yml` drift step) and `check_terraform_tree_currency` (`terraform-drift.yml:112`) keep their existing owner.\n- Extend `_WIRED_GATES` in `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py:27-30` to the full list of 28 lint-target scripts (the 25 `make lint` rows of table (3) + `check_adr_numbers`, `check_docs_index`, `check_verify_gate_parity`); its two parametrized tests replace every deleted per-twin wiring test, so wiring has exactly one census.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py` is untouched. Remove the imports and constants each deletion leaves unused (ruff F401/F841 names them).\n- The `test_check_adr_numbers_heldout.py`, `test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` and `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py` remainders stay as separate files here; the held-out epic (traitorous-official-sunbittern) merges them later.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the table (3) modules under `tests/unit/` and `tests/scripts/` (the spec counts 41 including the `_heldout`, `_lock_47e9` and `_red_proof` twins), `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`, `Makefile`. Out of scope: every `scripts/check_*.py` itself (no check script is edited, added, nor removed), every CI workflow file, `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py`, and the `_heldout` merges.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest --collect-only -q <the table (3) modules>` before: 688 nodes; after: 614 (688 − 74) plus 52 new census nodes (26 scripts × 2 parametrized tests added to `test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`); both counts recorded on this ticket. `make lint` exits 0 and its output lists `check_adr_numbers.py` and `check_docs_index.py --check`; `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No test under `tests/` invokes a `scripts/check_*.py` `main()`/`check()` against `REPO_ROOT`: `git grep -nE 'REPO_ROOT' -- tests | grep -E 'chk\\.main|gate\\.check|\\.main\\(\\[\\]\\)'` returns only `tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`.\n- [ ] Every `make lint` script appears in `_WIRED_GATES` and every `_WIRED_GATES` entry appears in `make -n lint` output — the census module's two parametrized tests pass over all 28 scripts (`pytest tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py`, 56 nodes).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` is gone (`git ls-files tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` prints nothing).\n- [ ] Node counts reconcile: 688 before, 614 + 52 after, from the two `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","id":"7300-7fab-807c-4ea0","parent_id":"f400-65b3-1899-4af9","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Give every scripts/check_*.py one owner in make lint and delete its real-tree pytest twins"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807175101442991,"uuid":"5a847b8e-dc30-4a8b-8fef-4a1ba547dd2a"}